  "body": "### What is the issue with the Compatibility Standard?\n\nhttps://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#ua-string-safari\n\n\nThis is currently display as:\n\n\"Mozilla/5.0 (<[safariPlatform](https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#safariplatform)>) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/<[safariVersion](https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#safariversion)><[deviceCompat](https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#devicecompat)>Safari/<[webkitVersion](https://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#webkitversion)>\"\n\n`Mozilla/5.0 (<safariPlatform>) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/<safariVersion><deviceCompat>Safari/<webkitVersion>`\n\nThere is \n* a missing space in between `<safariVersion>` and `<deviceCompat>`\n* Probably there should be a space after `<deviceCompat>` because if it doesn't exist. Then we get a `Version/<safariVersion>Safari/<webkitVersion>` which doesn't seem right either. \n\n",
